{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105435","id":2461548900,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6SuEFk","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105435","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105435.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105435.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105435","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105435/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105435/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105435/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/cd06e408acc7f2355ef764a0c4bd1e0dc7bda970","number":105435,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add Auto CPU/GPU sync mode (renderer low latency)","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Add CPU_GPU_SYNC_AUTO\r\nRemove redundant calls to get_ticks_usec()\r\n\r\nFixes an unrelated bug when NAVIGATION_2D_DISABLED or NAVIGATION_3D_DISABLED are defined.\r\n\r\nThis is a modified version of #100031\r\n\r\nNotable changes:\r\n\r\n1. Forbids the use of `CPU_GPU_SYNC_SEQUENTIAL` in production. It is allowed in the Editor, as it has its uses for debugging tight timing issues.\r\n2. Adds `CPU_GPU_SYNC_AUTO` which decides on realtime whether to use SEQUENTIAL or PARALLEL.\r\n    - AUTO is disabled on OpenGL. The timing was too unreliable and every time it switched between SEQ and PAR a very visible stutter would occur.\r\n    - AUTO has been tested by me on:\r\n        - Vulkan Linux AMD (Mesa RADV)\r\n        - Vulkan Windows AMD\r\n        - Vulkan Windows NVIDIA\r\n        - D3D12 Windows AMD\r\n        - D3D12 Windows NVIDIA\r\n3. Refactors the code as it lives in RenderingServer, since frame pacing is irrespective of implementation. It addresses the problems found [in this comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100031#issuecomment-2790860295). Frame Pacing code is a bit odd, because it involves very low level mechanisms (e.g. synchronization) but it needs to be aware of the engine as a whole at a very high level (in fact changes, albeit small, go all way to main.cpp).\r\n3. Adds monitors to debug and understand by AUTO decides to use SEQ or PAR.\r\n    - Those monitors are very useful even outside of frame pacing. They are very sensible to frame spikes and can detect issues that would cause stutter problems (even outside of AUTO/SEQ/PAR; as any frame time spike or hard missed target is very bad)\r\n\r\nThis is how the Monitors look like on a simple project, V-Sync enabled:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c6fb279a-0f23-4b72-93c6-02e6b9a0798b)\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archiv